From bae8bbe067b0fd44a9a482076b87534da63a5f37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:27:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: adopt hint binds this turn's chat;
 notify-subscribe names the chat it binds (agent-884fdd96f8)

adopt_next_step read HERMES_SESSION_ID from os.environ. A gateway/Desktop backend serving
several chats keeps whichever chat wrote it last there, so the kanban_origin_adopt hint told
chat aaaaaa to run notify-subscribe --chat-id bbbbbb (an unrelated chat). It now reads the
session ContextVar (get_session_env) unless an explicit env is passed.

notify-subscribe --platform tui prints the target chat's title from state.db and, when the
calling agent's chat (HERMES_SESSION_KEY/ID in its env, compared by compression tip) is a
different chat, a WARNING line naming it, so a wrong bind is visible at the command.
